{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1504","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1504","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1504\",\"parent_revision\":\"16b364e5464f57757dd420c733994e5c3b3125774b5a06e72dd345d47ef6e605\",\"root_revision\":\"16b364e5464f57757dd420c733994e5c3b3125774b5a06e72dd345d47ef6e605\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nserver.py lines 52-57 initialize the `TaskBackend` at module import time using a try/except around `get_task_config()` / `set_task_config(TaskConfig(backend=create_task_backend()))`. A comment at line 53 acknowledges that tests must call `set_task_config()` before importing the server module \u2014 fragile test-ordering discipline. FastMCP provides a `lifespan` context manager for startup/shutdown lifecycle, making the backend available as `ctx.lifespan_context[\\\"backend\\\"]` in every tool call and enabling clean teardown. Future backends holding connections or file locks have no shutdown hook in the current design.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**VERIFIED** \u2014 Module-level initialization exists as described, with minor line number discrepancy. Evidence:\\n\\n- Lines 52-57 of `server.py`:\\n  ```python\\n  # Initialize the default backend at module import time.\\n  # Tests may call set_task_config() before importing this module to inject a custom backend.\\n  try:\\n      get_task_config()\\n  except RuntimeError:\\n      set_task_config(TaskConfig(backend=create_task_backend()))\\n  ```\\n  The issue cited \\\"line 59 for the comment\\\" \u2014 the comment is at line 53. Minor discrepancy; the structural claim is correct.\\n- No `@contextlib.asynccontextmanager` lifespan or `mcp = FastMCP(..., lifespan=...)` anywhere in `server.py`.\\n- `_active_config` module-level mutable state exists in `task_config.py` (imported by server); `set_task_config` / `reset_task_config` mutate it.\\n- `test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` fixture at lines 130-157 uses `set_task_config(TaskConfig(backend=mock_backend))` + `reset_task_config()` in teardown \u2014 confirming the test-ordering fragility is already worked around but remains a discipline requirement.\\n\\n**Constraint noted**: The `backend_mock` fixture in `test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` currently relies on `set_task_config` / `reset_task_config` for injection. Migrating to lifespan requires updating the test fixture to use FastMCP's lifespan test utilities (e.g., `async_client` with a custom lifespan override), or retaining `set_task_config` as an escape hatch for tests.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: **refactor** (correctness of design without behavior change)\\n\\nRoot-Cause Analysis: Initial implementation used module-level state as the simplest path to get tools working. FastMCP lifespan was added to FastMCP after the initial implementation. No blocking technical reason exists to maintain module-level init \u2014 the `_active_config` pattern serves the same purpose as lifespan context but without lifecycle guarantees.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py:52\u201357` \u2014 init block to remove; lifespan to add\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py:60\u201383` \u2014 `_get_backend` helper to update (reads from lifespan context)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_config.py` \u2014 `set_task_config` / `reset_task_config` may be retained as test-only escape hatch or removed if lifespan test utilities are sufficient\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py:130\u2013157` \u2014 `backend_mock` fixture requires update\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Test ordering fragility**: tests that import `sam_schema.server` before calling `set_task_config` get a real backend \u2014 this is currently mitigated by the `backend_mock` fixture but requires developer discipline.\\n- **No shutdown hook**: backends that hold file locks, DB connections, or open handles have no place to release resources.\\n- **Harder to compose**: lifespan-based backends are the FastMCP idiom for server composition; module-level state diverges from that pattern.\\n- Severity: medium (no functional bug today, but a maintainability risk as backend complexity grows).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #1503 (ctx:Context injection) should be done first or concurrently \u2014 lifespan context and `ctx` parameter are complementary and cleaner to add together.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `mcp = FastMCP(\\\"sam\\\", ..., lifespan=_sam_lifespan)` declared with an async lifespan context manager\\n- [ ] `_sam_lifespan` calls `create_task_backend()`, stores it in `ctx.lifespan_context[\\\"backend\\\"]`, and on exit calls `backend.close()` if the backend exposes a `close()` method\\n- [ ] `_get_backend` (or equivalent) retrieves the backend from `ctx.lifespan_context[\\\"backend\\\"]` when `plan_dir` is the sentinel, rather than from module-level `get_task_config()`\\n- [ ] Module-level try/except init block (lines 52-57) removed\\n- [ ] `test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` `backend_mock` fixture updated to inject via lifespan override (or retained `set_task_config` escape hatch documented as test-only)\\n- [ ] All existing tests in `test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` pass after the refactor\\n- [ ] `run_server()` entry point unchanged \u2014 lifespan is transparent to the runner\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: **M**\\nReasoning: Mechanical refactor of init + `_get_backend` + lifespan wiring, but test fixture migration for the mock-backend injection pattern requires care. Need to verify FastMCP's lifespan test utilities work with the existing in-memory transport pattern used by `test_server_sam_taskbackend.py`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nObservable as a design smell:\\n\\n```bash\\ngrep -n \\\"module import time\\\\|set_task_config\\\\|get_task_config\\\" \\\\\\n  plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py\\n```\\n\\nShows the init block at lines 52-57 and confirms no lifespan registration.\\n\\nTest fragility: if a test imports `sam_schema.server` before calling `set_task_config`, it gets the real `LocalYamlTaskProvider` rather than a mock.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want **SAM server backend initialization to use FastMCP lifespan** so that **test ordering fragility is eliminated and backends with connections or locks have a clean shutdown hook**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: FastMCP review of P912 \u2014 .tmp/scratch/reports/fastmcp-review-P912.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6c13f1c72ee22de2260fffddb6380dc05698c3f4764324756bd20c2699cdf0db\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdr6hw\"}"}